# Remove an obstacle spawned at runtime via SpawnStatic / SpawnDynamic.
#
# `id` is what that call returned: the entity's `sim_path`, not its bare name. The two
# differ - the adapter registers world objects under an env-prefixed path - and taking the
# name here would fail to match for exactly the entities this service exists to remove.
#
# Any obstacle the human simulator knows resolves, world and scenario furniture included.
# A removed world-layer entity is not restored on reset.
string id
---
bool success
# False when nothing was removed: the id resolved to nothing, or the backend refused it.
bool found
string error_msg
